'''Chilled Ground''' is a detrimental [[ground effect]] that inflicts [[chill]]. 

__TOC__

==Mechanics==
Like regular [[chill]], chilled ground reduces [[action speed]], modifying the speed of the enemy's animations.<ref name="ChilledGround"/> Unless otherwise specified, chilled ground slows for 10%. Since version 3.9.0, the magnitude of chilled ground from map mods are 10%/20%/30% dependent on map tier. The actual magnitude of chill will be shown in the status icon, once the player character has stepped on the Chilled Ground and affected by it.

Chilled ground created by a player is affected by modifiers to the effect of cold and/or non-damaging ailments, including from the player's stats and [[support gem]]s. Chilled ground never counts as chills inflicted by the player. It ''cannot'' apply ''chilled by you'' stats, cannot make the player count as having chilled recently and can chill regardless of stats that prevent the application of chill by the player, such as {{il|Elemental Focus}} or {{psl|Secrets of Suffering}}. 

==Sources==
* {{il|Arctic Armour}} (while moving)
* {{il|Cold Snap}} (leave Chilled Ground that deals Cold DOT and chill ailment)
* {{il|Frostblink}}
* {{il|Frost Blades of Katabasis}}
* {{sl|id=Icestorm}}
* {{il|Aquamarine Flask}}
* {{il|Nuro's Harp}}
* {{il|The Brine Crown}}
* [[Shrine|Freezing Shrines]]
* Maps with the '[[of Ice]]' suffix
* Delve area mods
* Synthesis area mods
* Various monster skills
* [[Essence of Hatred]] monster modifier

Note that although similar, [[Chilling Area]]s are not necessarily considered chilled ground. {{il|Vortex}} is, but {{il|Creeping Frost}} and {{il|Frost Shield}} are not.

==Variations==
===Vortex ground===
Vortex ground is a type of chilled ground that also inflicts Cold Damage over Time. Multiple sources of Vortex ground do not stack. It uses the {{sl|id=Vortex}} skill icon as the status icon. 

* Enemy versions of {{il|Vortex}}
* Shaper-influenced ground effects and Volatile Anomalies
* [[Unstable Weta]]'s on-death effect
* [[Essence of Sorrow]] monster modifier
* Permafrost [[Archnemesis modifier]] before [[version 3.19.1c]])

===Cold Snap ground ===
Cold Snap ground is a type of chilled ground that also inflicts Cold Damage over Time. Multiple sources of Cold Snap ground do not stack. It uses the {{sl|id=ColdSnap}} skill icon as the status icon. 
* Enemy versions of {{il|Cold Snap}}/{{il|Vaal Cold Snap}}
* Delirium monster modifier

==Skill gems==
{{Drop enabled gem table
|where = items.class_id="Active Skill Gem"
  AND (skill.description LIKE "%Chilled Ground%" OR skill.description LIKE "%whirling vortex%")
}}

==Support gems==
{{Drop enabled gem table
|where = items.class_id="Support Skill Gem"
  AND (skill.description LIKE "%Chilled Ground%")
}}

==Unique items==
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|tables=item_stats
|join=items._pageID=item_stats._pageID
|where=
  item_stats.id LIKE "%chill%ground%"
|level=1
|large=1
|stat=1
}}
==Related modifiers==
===Item mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=1 AND (mod_stats.id LIKE "%chilled%ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%chilled ground%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}

* {{il|Essence of Insanity}}: {{ml|MovementSpeedOnBurningChilledShockedGroundEssence1|display=stat_text}} (boots only)

===Map mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=5 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%chilled ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%ice%" )
|spawn_weights=1
}}
The magnitude of the chill varies depending on the map tier: 
{{#cargo_query: 
|tables=mods, mod_stats, spawn_weights
|fields = CONCAT('[[', mods._pageName, '|', mods.name, ']]')=Name, spawn_weights.tag, mod_stats.max=Action Speed % reduction
|join on = mods._pageName=mod_stats._pageName, mods._pageName=spawn_weights._pageName 
|where = mods.domain=5 
 AND mods.id LIKE "MapChilledGround%" 
 AND mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%ice%base%"
 AND spawn_weights.weight > 0
 AND (
     spawn_weights.tag="low_tier_map"
  OR spawn_weights.tag="mid_tier_map"
  OR spawn_weights.tag="top_tier_map"
  OR spawn_weights.tag="secret_area"
)
|group by = mods._pageName, mod_stats.id
|order by = mods._pageName, mod_stats.id
}}
====Legacy map mods====
The following map mods can only be found in legacy map item in permanent leagues:
{{Modifier table
|q_tables = mod_stats, mod_spawn_weights
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_stats._pageID, mods._pageID=mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where = mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%ice%" AND domain = 5
|q_having = SUM(mod_spawn_weights.value) = 0
|q_groupBy = mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|stat_text=1
|level=1
|generation_type =1
|spawn_weights=1
}}
Note that the legacy mods do not have magnitude, it use the default value instead.

===Delve area mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=17 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%chilled ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%ice%" )
|spawn_weights=1
}}
===Synthesis area mods===
Synthesis map mods can only appear in Synthesis area
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=18 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%chilled ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%ice%" )
|spawn_weights=1
}}

==Trivia==
The ground effect shared the same graphic icon with [[chill]]ed ailment, [[Fearful]] debuff and [[Snow Cloak]] buff. The descriptive texts are not the same however.

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.0|
* Chilled ground from the Permafrost Archnemesis modifier now counts as Vortex ground, and can no longer stack with other sources of Vortex ground.
* Unstable Wetas now leave Vortex ground effect on death, instead of Cold Snap ground, and cannot stack with other sources of Vortex ground effect.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.15.0|
* User Interface Changes: Non-damaging Elemental Ailments applied to you or Enemies now display their effect.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.1f|
* Improved the visibility of Chilled Ground.{{efn|name=actual change}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.0|
* Improved the appearance of shocked, burning, caustic and chilled ground.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.9.0|
* Shock and Chill calculations have been changed. In general, it is much easier to Shock and Chill monsters with low values of the ailment, but harder to reach high values of Shock and Chill. The formula used to calculate Shock and Chill magnitudes is now: 1/2*[Damage % of Ailment Threshold (see below)]^0.4
* We've added an Ailment Threshold to monsters. In the great majority of cases, the Ailment Threshold matches the monster's Maximum Life. It primarily differs for especially high-life monsters (such as The Shaper), where the threshold is reduced to allow ailments to be applied with hits that wouldn't ordinarily reach the required Life thresholds.
* The Map and Area mods have changed. It now has a stat id "map_ground_ice_base_magnitude", which default is 20/35/50 (unit: %) depends on tier. The stat id is the magnitude of chill inflicted by the ground effect. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.1.0|
* Map mods have also been rebalanced, and every mod now provides increased item rarity, increased item quantity, and increased monster pack size, though the magnitudes are dependent on the difficulty of the mod.
* New [[of Ice]] map mods were introduced. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.0.0|
* Chilled ground has a fixed slowing effect of 10%.
* Other non-hit sources of Chill, unless otherwise specified in the debuff, will slow by 10%.
}}
{{Version history table row|2.1.0|
* We've made performance improvements to ground effects. They now use considerably less bandwidth and server resources. Disconnections or lockstep stuttering near ground effects should occur far less often.
}}
{{Version history table row|1.0.0|
* The new Ground Ice looks awesome.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.10.2|
* Improved the performance of Ground Ice and Ground Tar.
* Improved the audio for ground effects, gore effects and Pyromaniac projectiles.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.10.0|
* The "Chilled" statuses from cold damage and ground ice do not stack any more.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.9|
* Added support for ground fire and other environmental hazards.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

